# GPU firmware must be in the FIRST-STAGE initramfs.
#
# DRM_MSM is built in, and on a7xx the adreno driver loads its SQE microcode
# at component-bind time — t≈1.0s, long before the rootfs is mounted. A
# firmware miss there is FATAL for the whole boot's GPU: adreno gives up, msm
# registers display-only (debugfs 'gpu' node reads ENODEV), and nothing
# retries later. Observed exactly that on r39: "Direct firmware load for
# qcom/a730_sqe.fw failed with error -2" at 0.99s, /dev/dri/renderD128
# present but dead.
#
# SQE + GMU come from linux-firmware-qcom (zstd-compressed; the kernel has
# FW_LOADER_COMPRESS_ZSTD). The zap shader is Samsung-signed and ships in the
# device's apnhlos partition — it is staged into /lib/firmware by hand (see
# tools/README), NOT by any package, so those entries carry !optional: a
# rootfs build without the staged zap must not fail, but the resulting
# initramfs will boot a GPU-less (display-only) msm. Check for the zap
# after any rootfs rebuild.
/lib/firmware/qcom/a730_sqe.fw.zst
/lib/firmware/qcom/gmu_gen70000.bin.zst
/lib/firmware/qcom/sm8450/gts8pwifi/a730_zap.mdt!optional
/lib/firmware/qcom/sm8450/gts8pwifi/a730_zap.b00!optional
/lib/firmware/qcom/sm8450/gts8pwifi/a730_zap.b01!optional
/lib/firmware/qcom/sm8450/gts8pwifi/a730_zap.b02!optional
